      "message": "fix(wire): a work bottom at the lower guide is within reach\n\nThe guide-reach law compared the work with each guide plane strictly.\nAn origin at the part bottom and a lower guide at Z0 differ only by\nround-off (the origin comes from a box, the facets from their own\ntransform), and the post was blocked with \"work bottom Z-0.000 is\nbelow the lower guide Z0.000\". The law now compares within\nGUIDE_REACH_TOL (wire_edm::PATH_TOL, 10 nm) in the wire laws' span\ncheck, the tapered pose check and the Agie job check. The messages\nnever print \"-0.000\"; a refused gap that reads as zero in three\ndecimals is written with six. A real gap is still refused by name.\n\nFixes #4039\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
